## Product thesis — keep edits in this lane

Own the construction-in-progress → placed-in-service (CIP → PIS) determination-and-defense
layer: the ASC 360 / 835-20 capitalization judgment between project-cost systems and the
GL. Deliberate non-scope: not a Workiva replacement (no XBRL/EDGAR/MD&A), not enterprise
planning.

## Shared conventions — these apply everywhere

- **The ERP is the system of record.** Korvyn reads it and adds visibility, workflow,
  controls, close, reconciliation, analytics and AI. **Never build journal-entry creation,
  approval, or posting.** (`packages/core` *models* journal entries because validating and
  reconciling them requires representing them faithfully — that is not posting.)
- **Numbers derive, never duplicate.** If a figure appears in two places, derive it once.
  Never scale sample data into a headline (see the `RECON_SCALE` cautionary tale in
  `apps/dashboard/CLAUDE.md`).
- **No dead controls.** If an affordance cannot act, do not add it. An unexported handler
  behind an `onclick` is a dead control. So is a control that silently disappears with no
  explanation of why.
- **AI narrates, never computes a number.** Every figure comes from an engine or a tool;
  the AI layer only explains and cites.
- **The single-file apps stay single-file** (`index.html`, `apps/*`): no build step, no
  external runtime dependencies.
- **Work incrementally.** Never rebuild or redesign an existing page unless asked.

## Toolchain

Node is installed but **not on `PATH`** — it lives at `C:\Users\mitragiri\tools\node22\`
(v22, npm bundled). Prepend it or things look broken:

```powershell
$env:Path = "C:\Users\mitragiri\tools\node22;$env:Path"
```

Before concluding a tool is absent, search the filesystem, not just `PATH`. Python is also
available.

## Checks

```bash
node tools/check_chrome_themes.mjs     # index.html chrome themes pass WCAG AA (10 themes)
cd packages/core && npm run check      # typecheck + tests + the import-boundary checker
cd packages/agent && npm run dryrun    # all tools resolve, no API call
```

For `index.html` the browser sweep is the end-to-end check: open it, drive every tab,
assert each view rendered, console clean.
